  "description": {
    "text": "A box from November 2010 that held one of the four 2010 World Championships decks and nine holo Pikachu cards, each in a different language: English, Italian, Korean, Spanish, Japanese, German, French, Polish and Portuguese. Eight of them show Pikachu in a scene from their language's country, the English one before the Grand Canyon; the Japanese card has Ken Sugimori's Pikachu on a plain holo background. All nine have gold holofoil borders and a PW mark, and the box turns to show every card.\n\nThe same nine cards came out first in Japan, on 8 July 2010, in Pokémon Center and 7-Eleven binders. This box's cards differ from Japan's in their backs, English here and Japanese there, and in the copyright line at the foot of the card: ©2010 Pokémon/Nintendo on this box's, ©2010 Pokémon/Nintendo/Creatures/GAME FREAK on Japan's.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "PokéZentrum: Pikachu World Collection, Kartenliste und Guide für Sammler",
        "url": "https://pokezentrum.de/?p=105539"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: Pikachu world collection 2010 - Questions",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/pikachu-world-collection-2010-questions/15147"
      },
      {
        "title": "PocketMonsters.net: Pokémon Card Game Pikachu World Set (2010)",
        "url": "https://pocketmonsters.net/index.php/forum/thread/2989"
      },
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: World Collection (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 22 July 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260722074933/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Pikachu_World_(TCG)"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "A \"PW\" symbol at the bottom right, and no number",
    "sources": [
